[center][size=6][color=#00ccff][b]AbsoluteHOTAS 4.0.2[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][b][color=#ffaa00]Stable RTSS compatibility hotfix[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[line]

4.0.2 supersedes 4.0.1 as the recommended main file. It fixes a workbench
regression with RivaTuner Statistics Server and similar software that maintains
ownership of the DXGI/D3D12 render-hook chain after startup.

[list]
[*][b]RTSS compatibility restored:[/b] AbsoluteHOTAS now chains behind a detected existing render detour instead of competing for the public DXGI function prologue.[/*]
[*][b]No shadow vtable:[/b] The fix does not copy, replace, or assume the size of a swapchain vtable.[/*]
[*][b]Reliable workbench inputs:[/b] Both the configured HOTAS workbench button and [b]Ctrl+Alt+B[/b] are polled independently of render callbacks.[/*]
[*][b]Locally validated:[/b] RTSS 7.3.5.28314 was loaded first with its global D3D12/DXGI hook enabled; the workbench initialized, rendered, closed, and reopened cleanly through both inputs.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Updating from 4.0.1:[/b] install the 4.0.2 archive normally. Keep
[b]AbsoluteHOTAS_Custom.ini[/b] and the [b]Profiles[/b] directory; they contain
user-owned settings and are not included in the archive.

RTSS and comparable Windows overlay/capture hooks are a compatibility priority
for this hotfix. Linux/Proton and third-party frame generation remain best effort.
If a graphics combination still conflicts with the workbench, set
[b][UI] bEnableWorkbench = false[/b]; flight controls and manual configuration
continue without renderer hooks.

